# Part E: Applegate--Lagarias multiplier identity (x = -1 mod 2^k, odd j <= k, m_j = (2^j+1)/3)
  U(m_j x) = oddpart(x + (x+1)/2^j) in 310/310 checks; m_j = (2^j+1)/3 satisfies 3 m_j - 1 = 2^j (the 3x-1 trunk); examples [(3, 1, 1, 7, 11, 11), (3, 1, 1, 15, 23, 23), (3, 1, 1, 23, 35, 35), (3, 1, 1, 31, 47, 47)]
  descent factor of the one-step image: (x + (x+1)/2^j)/x -> 1 + 2^-j: the multiplier resets the binary tail (x' = -1 mod 2^(k-j) only).
